  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Drier weather, featuring cool overnights and \nwarm afternoons.\n\nClear skies this afternoon will persist into Saturday with a\nmuch drier airmass now in place over the region. Strong surface\nlow over the Atlantic will continue to strengthen and move \nnorth through Sunday morning. Model guidance does indicate that \nthe low may retrograde west on Sunday and stall along the New \nJersey coast through Monday. This appears to be close enough \nto bring some cloudiness to the forecast area on Sunday and \nMonday. Have also added a mention of showers along the I64 \ncorridor given enough guidance showing some potential for \nshowers to reach the area.\n\nLow pressure will lift north and weaken by Tuesday as high\npressure then begins to build over the eastern CONUS. Should see\nincreasingly warmer temperatures through next week given\nincreasing heights and return flow. Other than some isolated\nshowers Sun/Mon, dry conditions will likely continue through at\nleast Thursday next week.",
